    <item>
      <title>The Unyielding Wrath of Narakasura</title>
      <description>Today&apos;s story will change how you see everything... In the city of Dwarka, Prince Narakasura was born with a curse that made his wrath unstoppable. His father, the god Vishnu, had promised to protect him from his own anger, but Narakasura&apos;s jealousy of his parents&apos; love for their other children grew stronger every day. He became a tyrant, enslaving the people of Dwarka and killing anyone who dared to oppose him. His parents, who had loved him so dearly, were now forced to flee for their lives. The people of Dwarka, in desperation, cried out for help. The gods, who had grown tired of Narakasura&apos;s cruelty, sent their greatest warrior, Krishna, to defeat the prince. The battle raged on for days, with Narakasura&apos;s wrath fueling his strength. But Krishna, who had once been a friend to Narakasura, now saw him as an enemy. He fought with a fierce determination, pushing Narakasura to his limits. Finally, the prince&apos;s rage consumed him, and he became a monster, attacking everyone in sight. But Krishna, with a heavy heart, ended Narakasura&apos;s life, putting an end to the prince&apos;s wrath. This is Wrath — the uncontrolled anger that destroys everything in its path. Today, we see the same destructive force in our own world, where hatred and intolerance rage on, fueled by a desire for power and control.</description>
